1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,250
Every year, Ethiopians travel to Kulubi for Saint Gabriel. That year, my family went too.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:13,700
Five of us, packed into our old Elantra, with 525 kilometres ahead.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,950
At Awash, camels crossed the road as if they owned it.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,580
Monkeys watched us from the roadside, curious about the travellers.

5
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:34,180
Near Asbe Teferi, the land rose into dark volcanic rock and mountains.

6
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,540
Then the road dropped toward the lowlands, and the heat came with it.

7
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,580
Our old car could not take it. Steam rose from the engine.

8
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:55,710
Every few kilometres we stopped, and my father poured water on the engine to cool it.

9
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:03,430
That is what I remember most: all of us, waiting together by the road.

10
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:10,020
Slowly, stop by stop, we reached Dire Dawa.

11
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:19,450
And at Kulubi, among thousands in white, we stood together before Saint Gabriel.
